---
import ContentPage from "../layouts/ContentPage.astro";
import { ORG_EMAIL } from "../lib/seo";

const site = "https://refocus.co.in";
const UPDATED = "2026-10-11";
const mailto = `mailto:${ORG_EMAIL}`;
const title = "Community Guidelines";
const description =
  "How to be a good focus partner on Refocus: session etiquette, respect and safety, privacy, community posts, and how we handle reports.";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: "Community Guidelines — Refocus",
    url: `${site}/community-guidelines`,
    description,
    dateModified: new Date(UPDATED).toISOString(),
  },
];
---

<ContentPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="/community-guidelines"
  heading="Community Guidelines"
  updated={UPDATED}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    Refocus works because people show up for each other. When you book a
    session, someone else is planning their time around you. These guidelines
    describe what that looks like in practice, so every session feels safe,
    focused, and worth showing up for. They sit alongside our
    <a href="/terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> and
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Show up on time, or let your partner know early if you can't.</li>
    <li>Say what you'll work on, then actually work on it.</li>
    <li>Be kind, keep it about focus, and respect people's privacy.</li>
    <li>If something feels wrong, block and report. We take it seriously.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>During a session</h2>
  <h3>Be on time</h3>
  <p>
    Join when the session starts. Your partner has set aside this time, and a
    late or missing partner makes the whole session harder. If your plans
    change, cancel as early as you can so your partner can be matched with
    someone else. Once a session with a partner has started, it can no longer
    be cancelled or left from your calendar, so please plan ahead.
  </p>

  <h3>Start with a goal</h3>
  <p>
    Take a moment at the start to share what you plan to get done, and check in
    briefly at the end. Saying it out loud is a big part of what makes body
    doubling work. Keep both short; the time in between is for working.
  </p>

  <h3>Keep your camera on and your space appropriate</h3>
  <p>
    Seeing each other work is what creates the accountability, so keep your
    camera on for the session unless you and your partner have agreed
    otherwise. Make sure what's on camera is something you'd be comfortable
    with in a shared library or co-working space: dress appropriately and keep
    your surroundings work-friendly.
  </p>

  <h3>Respect quiet mode and noise</h3>
  <p>
    Some people book quiet sessions and start muted. Follow their lead, keep
    your microphone muted while working if there's background noise, and save
    conversation for the start and end of the session.
  </p>

  <h3>Do focused work</h3>
  <p>
    Sessions are for work, study, or a personal project you want to make
    progress on. They're not for selling, recruiting, dating, or long social
    chats. If you'd like to get to know a regular partner better, add them as a
    friend and talk outside of sessions.
  </p>

  <h2>Respect and safety</h2>
  <p>
    Refocus is for everyone who wants to get things done, whatever their
    background. We don't allow:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Harassment, threats, bullying, or intimidation of any kind.</li>
    <li>Hate speech or discrimination based on who someone is.</li>
    <li>
      Sexual content, sexual comments, or unwanted advances, in sessions, chat,
      or posts.
    </li>
    <li>Violent, graphic, or illegal content.</li>
    <li>Impersonating someone else or misrepresenting who you are.</li>
    <li>
      Spam, scams, advertising, or repeatedly promoting your own products or
      services.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Don't record, screenshot, or share sessions</strong> without your
      partner's clear permission.
    </li>
    <li>
      Don't ask for or share personal information such as addresses, phone
      numbers, or financial details.
    </li>
    <li>
      What your partner says or shows during a session stays in that session.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Friends, chat, and community posts</h2>
  <p>
    The same standards apply everywhere on Refocus, not just in sessions.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Only send friend and session requests to people you'd like to work with,
      and accept a "no" or no reply gracefully.
    </li>
    <li>
      In the community feed, share progress, wins, questions, and
      encouragement. Keep posts on topic: focus, study, work, goals, and habits.
    </li>
    <li>
      Disagree respectfully. Criticise ideas, not people, and don't pile on.
    </li>
    <li>Don't post private messages or other people's information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Looking after yourself</h2>
  <p>
    Refocus is a productivity tool, not a substitute for professional support.
    If you're struggling with your mental health or feel unsafe, please reach
    out to a local helpline or emergency service. If a partner says something
    that makes you worried for their safety, tell us at
    <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Blocking and reporting</h2>
  <p>
    If someone makes you uncomfortable, you don't need to explain yourself.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Leave the call</strong> at any point if you feel unsafe. Your
      safety matters more than finishing the session.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Block</strong> the person, so you won't be matched with them or
      hear from them again.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Report</strong> the person, post, or comment from the product.
      Reports go to the Refocus team and are kept private.
    </li>
    <li>
      For anything you can't report in the product, email
      <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What happens when guidelines are broken</h2>
  <p>
    We review reports and act based on how serious the issue is and whether it
    has happened before. Depending on the situation, we may:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Remove the content.</li>
    <li>Send a warning.</li>
    <li>Temporarily mute someone in the community.</li>
    <li>Ban someone from the community, or from booking sessions.</li>
    <li>Close the account permanently.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Serious harm, such as threats, sexual misconduct, or exploitation, can lead
    to an immediate permanent ban. Repeatedly not showing up for booked
    sessions can also limit how many sessions you can book.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    These guidelines will evolve as the community grows. If you have a question
    or a suggestion, write to us at <a href={mailto}>{ORG_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
